{"parseRefreshTokenResponse returns the full Zod safeParse result (containing success and data fields) rather than the parsed token data itself, causing invalid shape to be stored in database and breaking subsequent token usage": 0.8787228465080261, "refreshOAuthTokens wrapper returns inconsistent shape (Response vs JSON) - conditionally returns raw response from fetch/axios when callers expect a token object with properties like access_token and expiry_date, breaking token refresh flows for Google Calendar, Office 365, Zoom, etc.": 0.6906774640083313, "Encryption code uses AES-256 CBC without integrity check (no MAC/HMAC), meaning ciphertext could be tampered with without detection, potentially leading to invalid decryptions or credential leakage": 0.42305296659469604, "Credential Prisma model does not declare a unique constraint on the composite (userId, appId) key, allowing multiple credentials to exist for the same user and app, undermining canonical credential per user-app": 0.40781328082084656, "Documentation in .env.example incorrectly specifies CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY length - states 32 bytes required for AES-256 but suggested command uses openssl rand -base64 24 which yields only 24 raw bytes": 0.8588287234306335, "Webhook header name handling may fail if env defines non-lowercase header - req.headers lookup doesn't normalize header name to lower-case, causing potential 403s from misconfiguration": 0.7852866649627686}